---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const title = 'BI Dashboard Audit | Aesop Analytics'
const description = 'Think your dashboards are the problem? A BI dashboard audit that looks past the charts to what actually breaks trust — conflicting definitions, no owners, manual rebuilds — and the governed system that keeps the fix true. Start with a free diagnostic.'
const ogDescription = "Most 'bad dashboards' are good dashboards built on numbers no one trusts. Here is the honest version of a dashboard audit — and what keeps the fix from unraveling.";

const auditSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  serviceType: "BI dashboard audit",
  name: "BI Dashboard Audit",
  description:
    "A reporting audit that looks past dashboard design to what actually breaks trust: conflicting KPI definitions, missing ownership, untrusted sources, and manual rebuilds. Delivered as the fixed-fee Reporting Clarity Assessment, and kept true by Aesop Manteia, a governed data-practice platform.",
  provider: { "@type": "ProfessionalService", name: "Aesop Analytics", url: "https://aesopanalytics.com" },
  areaServed: "US",
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/bi-dashboard-audit" ogDescription={ogDescription} schema={auditSchema}>

<!-- HERO -->
<section class="lp-hero reface ae-host ae-mark" style="--ae-size:min(40vw,470px); --ae-right:-2%; --ae-top:-18%; --ae-opacity:.07;">
  <div class="lp-in">
    <div class="eyebrow">BI Dashboard Audit</div>
    <h1>You came looking for a dashboard audit.</h1>
    <p class="dek">Here's the honest version: the dashboard is rarely the real problem. Most "bad dashboards" are perfectly good dashboards built on numbers nobody trusts — and a redesign doesn't fix that. What fixes it is auditing the reporting underneath, then leaving behind a governed system that keeps the numbers true.</p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a href="/diagnostic/?utm_source=site&utm_medium=internal&utm_campaign=bda-hero-diagnostic" class="btn">Book a diagnostic</a>
      <a href="/resources/dashboard-audit/" class="btn ghost">Try the free checklist first</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- THE REFRAME -->
<section class="lp-band reface">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="lp-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="sec-label">The real problem</div>
        <h2>A prettier chart can't fix a number people don't believe.</h2>
        <p>When leadership stops trusting a dashboard, the instinct is to rebuild it — cleaner layout, better visuals, a new tool. But the distrust almost never comes from the chart. It comes from underneath, from questions a redesign never touches:</p>
        <div class="pov">Most reporting problems are not visualization problems. They are ownership, definition, process, trust, and governance problems.</div>
        <p>Audit the dashboard and you fix the symptom. Audit the reporting behind it — and put a governed record around what you find — and you fix the cause.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="lp-listlabel">What's usually actually wrong</div>
        <div class="lp-list">
          <div class="lp-item"><span class="i">↯</span><span>Two teams define the same KPI differently — so two dashboards disagree, and both are "right"</span></div>
          <div class="lp-item"><span class="i">↯</span><span>No one owns the metric, so no one can settle which number is official</span></div>
          <div class="lp-item"><span class="i">↯</span><span>The dashboard is rebuilt by hand each cycle from exports nobody reconciles</span></div>
          <div class="lp-item"><span class="i">↯</span><span>The source data is mistrusted, so the dashboard is mistrusted by extension</span></div>
          <div class="lp-item"><span class="i">↯</span><span>Five dashboards exist for one function and nobody knows which is current</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- WHAT A REAL AUDIT COVERS -->
<section class="lp-cover reface">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-label">What a real audit covers</div>
    <h2>Past the charts, to what breaks trust.</h2>
    <p class="intro">A surface dashboard review grades visuals. A reporting audit maps the whole estate and finds where trust actually leaks — the work that lets leadership believe the number again. It's the same map the product builds from.</p>
    <div class="cover-grid">
      <div class="cov"><h3>The reporting estate</h3><p>Every dashboard, spreadsheet, and recurring report — inventoried, with what's used, what's ignored, and what's duplicated.</p></div>
      <div class="cov"><h3>Metric conflicts</h3><p>Exactly where definitions diverge across teams, the specific disagreement, and the business impact where it can be quantified.</p></div>
      <div class="cov"><h3>Ownership &amp; source of truth</h3><p>Which metrics have no owner, which system is authoritative, and where "whose number is right" arguments come from.</p></div>
      <div class="cov"><h3>Manual burden</h3><p>How many hours go into rebuilding reports by hand each cycle — the abstract "we do a lot of manual work" turned into a number.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="cover-foot">That's the <a href="/assessment/?utm_source=site&utm_medium=internal&utm_campaign=bda-cover-assessment">Reporting Clarity Assessment</a> — a fixed-fee reporting audit with ten deliverables and a prioritized 30/60/90-day roadmap. It's the version of a "dashboard audit" that actually changes whether leadership trusts the report — and it maps your estate into <a href="/platform/">Aesop Manteia</a>, so the fix doesn't quietly unravel the next quarter.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- THE GOVERNED FIX -->
<section class="lp-fix reface ae-host ae-mark" style="--ae-size:min(38vw,420px); --ae-left:-4%; --ae-bottom:-30%; --ae-opacity:.05;">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-label">Where the fix lives</div>
    <h2>The audit finds the gaps. The product keeps them closed.</h2>
    <p class="fix-intro">A one-time audit tells you the truth on the day it's delivered. Six months later, definitions drift, owners move on, and the dashboards quietly disagree again. Aesop Manteia is the living record that keeps a dashboard audit from expiring: your estate mapped from metadata, every metric's owner and definition in plain view, and the gaps rendered in red where no one owns them yet.</p>
    <div class="fix-rail">
      <div class="fr-item"><span class="fr-dot dep"></span><div><div class="fr-h">The governed portal is deployed</div><p>Log in and see a real, governed estate — owners, definitions, and what no one owns at all. The write layer is live too: ratify a definition, assign an owner, and the record updates.</p></div></div>
      <div class="fr-item"><span class="fr-dot prev"></span><div><div class="fr-h">Live-data querying is in preview</div><p>Asking your live data directly, and regenerating governed reports from the map, is the newest capability — ratified and building. We'll show you exactly how far along it is.</p></div></div>
    </div>
    <p class="fix-note">We say this plainly because it's the whole point: a company that sells trust should be honest about what its own product can and can't do yet.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- TWO WAYS -->
<section class="lp-two reface">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Two ways to start.</h2>
    <div class="two-grid">
      <div class="two-card">
        <div class="tc-tag">Free · self-serve</div>
        <h3>Dashboard Audit Checklist</h3>
        <p>Thirty scored questions you can run on your own reporting in fifteen minutes. A fast self-scan to see where the trust gaps are — no email required.</p>
        <a href="/resources/dashboard-audit/" class="lp-link">Open the checklist →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="two-card hl">
        <div class="tc-tag">Fixed fee · done with you</div>
        <h3>Reporting Clarity Assessment</h3>
        <p>The full audit: your estate inventoried, conflicts surfaced, ownership mapped into Manteia, and a prioritized roadmap. $5,000–$9,500, 2–3 weeks, starting with a free diagnostic.</p>
        <a href="/assessment/?utm_source=site&utm_medium=internal&utm_campaign=bda-ladder-assessment" class="lp-link">See the Assessment →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="two-proof">See what the fix looks like in practice — <a href="/work/">reporting modernization case studies</a>, anonymized with the result signals intact. For the broader picture, see <a href="/reporting-modernization-consulting/">reporting modernization consulting</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CTA -->
<section class="lp-cta reface">
  <div class="cta-in">
    <div class="eyebrow">Start here</div>
    <h2>Find out whether it's the dashboard — or the numbers under it.</h2>
    <p>A free 30-minute Reporting Trust Diagnostic. No pitch, no slide deck. We'll tell you honestly whether a redesign would help, or whether the real fix is upstream — and if Manteia isn't right for where you are, we'll say so.</p>
    <a href="/diagnostic/?utm_source=site&utm_medium=internal&utm_campaign=bda-closing-diagnostic" class="btn">Book a diagnostic</a>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
.lp-hero { background:var(--navy); padding:84px 0 64px; }
.lp-in { max-width:840px; margin:0 auto; padding:0 32px; }
.lp-hero .eyebrow { color:var(--twine); margin-bottom:16px; }
.lp-hero h1 { font-size:clamp(36px,5.4vw,64px); line-height:1.04; color:#fff; margin-bottom:20px; font-weight:600; }
.lp-hero .dek { font-size:19px; color:#C4BDAE; font-weight:300; line-height:1.6; max-width:62ch; margin-bottom:30px; }
.sec-label { font-weight:700; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.22em; font-size:11px; color:var(--twine); margin-bottom:16px; }
/* REFRAME BAND */
.lp-band { padding:72px 0; background:var(--paper); }
.lp-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:56px; align-items:start; }
@media(max-width:760px){ .lp-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:32px; } }
.lp-band h2 { margin-bottom:18px; line-height:1.1; }
.lp-band p { font-size:17px; color:var(--slate); line-height:1.65; font-weight:300; margin-bottom:16px; }
.lp-band .pov { font-family:"Newsreader",Georgia,serif; font-weight:400; font-style:italic; font-size:clamp(17px,2.1vw,22px); color:var(--navy); border-left:4px solid var(--twine); padding:8px 0 8px 22px; margin:24px 0; line-height:1.42; }
.lp-listlabel { font-size:11px; font-weight:700; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.22em; color:var(--twine); margin-bottom:18px; }
.lp-list { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:0; border-top:2px solid var(--rule); }
.lp-item { display:flex; gap:14px; align-items:flex-start; padding:15px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); font-size:16px; color:var(--ink); line-height:1.5; font-weight:400; }
.lp-item .i { color:var(--contessa); font-weight:700; flex-shrink:0; }
/* COVER */
.lp-cover { padding:72px 0; background:var(--paper-2); border-top:1px solid var(--rule); border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule); }
.lp-cover h2 { margin-bottom:14px; }
.lp-cover .intro { font-size:17px; color:var(--slate); font-weight:300; max-width:66ch; margin-bottom:40px; line-height:1.6; }
.cover-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr); gap:16px; }
@media(max-width:640px){ .cover-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
.cov { background:#fff; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:6px; padding:24px 22px; }
.cov h3 { font-size:16px; font-weight:700; color:var(--navy); margin-bottom:8px; font-family:"DM Sans",sans-serif; letter-spacing:0; }
.cov p { font-size:14.5px; color:var(--muted); line-height:1.55; font-weight:300; }
.cover-foot { font-size:17px; color:var(--slate); font-weight:300; line-height:1.65; max-width:72ch; margin-top:32px; }
.cover-foot a, .two-proof a { color:var(--sepia); text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:2px; }
/* THE GOVERNED FIX */
.lp-fix { background:var(--navy); padding:80px 0; }
.lp-fix .sec-label { color:var(--twine); }
.lp-fix h2 { color:#fff; margin-bottom:16px; max-width:22ch; }
.lp-fix .fix-intro { font-size:17px; color:#C4BDAE; font-weight:300; line-height:1.65; max-width:70ch; margin-bottom:36px; }
.fix-rail { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:24px; }
@media(max-width:720px){ .fix-rail { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
.fr-item { display:flex; gap:14px; align-items:flex-start; background:var(--navy-2); border-radius:8px; padding:24px 22px; }
.fr-dot { width:10px; height:10px; border-radius:50%; flex-shrink:0; margin-top:6px; }
.fr-dot.dep { background:var(--good); }
.fr-dot.prev { background:var(--warn); }
.fr-h { font-size:15px; font-weight:700; color:#fff; margin-bottom:7px; }
.fr-item p { font-size:14px; color:#B8C2D0; line-height:1.58; font-weight:300; }
.fix-note { font-size:14px; color:#8FA4B8; font-weight:300; line-height:1.6; max-width:68ch; margin-top:26px; }
/* TWO WAYS */
.lp-two { padding:72px 0; }
.lp-two h2 { margin-bottom:32px; }
.two-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:20px; }
@media(max-width:640px){ .two-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
.two-card { background:#fff; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:8px; padding:28px 26px; }
.two-card.hl { border-top:3px solid var(--twine); }
.tc-tag { font-size:11px; font-weight:700; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.16em; color:var(--twine); margin-bottom:12px; }
.two-card h3 { font-size:22px; color:var(--navy); margin-bottom:12px; }
.two-card p { font-size:15.5px; color:var(--slate); line-height:1.6; font-weight:300; margin-bottom:18px; }
.lp-link { font-size:14px; font-weight:700; color:var(--twine); letter-spacing:.03em; }
.lp-link:hover { color:var(--sepia); }
.two-proof { margin-top:28px; font-size:15px; color:var(--muted); line-height:1.6; font-weight:300; max-width:70ch; }
/* CTA */
.lp-cta { background:var(--navy); border-top:3px solid var(--twine); padding:80px 32px; text-align:center; }
.cta-in { max-width:680px; margin:0 auto; }
.lp-cta .eyebrow { color:var(--twine); margin-bottom:18px; display:block; }
.lp-cta h2 { color:#fff; margin-bottom:16px; line-height:1.08; }
.lp-cta p { color:#A8B4C0; font-size:17px; font-weight:300; max-width:56ch; margin:0 auto 30px; line-height:1.6; }
</style>

</BaseLayout>
